{"id":"mahabharata-3-266","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":266,"title":"षट्षष्ट्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 266 · Hanuman finds Sita","summary":{"en":"Rama waits on Mount Malyavat through the rains, and when Sugriva delays, Lakshmana rouses him; the monkeys search every quarter. Hanuman's party in the south learns of Lanka from Sampati, Hanuman leaps the ocean, finds Sita, burns the city and returns to Rama with her token.","kn":"ಮಳೆಗಾಲದಲ್ಲಿ ಶ್ರೀರಾಮನು ಮಾಲ್ಯವತ್ ಪರ್ವತದಲ್ಲಿ ಕಾಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಸುಗ್ರೀವನು ತಡಮಾಡಿದಾಗ ಲಕ್ಷ್ಮಣನು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕಪಿಗಳು ಎಲ್ಲ ದಿಕ್ಕುಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಹುಡುಕುತ್ತಾರೆ. ದಕ್ಷಿಣದ ಹನುಮಂತನ ತಂಡ ಸಂಪಾತಿಯಿಂದ ಲಂಕೆಯ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ತಿಳಿಯುತ್ತದೆ; ಹನುಮಂತನು ಸಮುದ್ರ ಲಂಘಿಸಿ ಸೀತೆಯನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ನಗರವನ್ನು ಸುಟ್ಟು ಅವಳ ಗುರುತಿನೊಂದಿಗೆ ಶ್ರೀರಾಮನ ಬಳಿಗೆ ಮರಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"श्रीराम वर्षा भर माल्यवान पर्वत पर प्रतीक्षा करते हैं, और सुग्रीव के देर करने पर लक्ष्मण उसे सचेत करते हैं; वानर हर दिशा में खोजते हैं। दक्षिण में हनुमान का दल सम्पाति से लंका के बारे में जानता है, हनुमान समुद्र लाँघकर सीता को खोजते हैं, नगर जलाते हैं और उनकी निशानी लेकर श्रीराम के पास लौटते हैं।","te":"వర్షాకాలమంతా శ్రీరాముడు మాల్యవత్ పర్వతంపై వేచి ఉంటాడు; సుగ్రీవుడు ఆలస్యం చేయగా లక్ష్మణుడు అతనిని మేల్కొల్పుతాడు; వానరులు అన్ని దిక్కుల్లో వెతుకుతారు. దక్షిణాన హనుమంతుని బృందం సంపాతి నుండి లంక గురించి తెలుసుకుంటుంది; హనుమంతుడు సముద్రం లంఘించి సీతను కనుగొని, నగరాన్ని దహించి, ఆమె గుర్తుతో శ్రీరాముని దగ్గరకు తిరిగివస్తాడు.","ta":"மழைக்காலம் முழுதும் ஸ்ரீராமர் மால்யவத் மலையில் காத்திருக்கிறார்; ஸுக்ரீவன் தாமதிக்க லக்ஷ்மணன் அவனைத் தூண்டுகிறான்; வானரங்கள் எல்லாத் திசைகளிலும் தேடுகின்றன. தெற்கில் ஹனுமானின் குழு ஸம்பாதியிடமிருந்து லங்கையைப் பற்றி அறிகிறது; ஹனுமான் கடலைத் தாண்டி ஸீதையைக் கண்டு நகரை எரித்து அவள் அடையாளத்துடன் ஸ்ரீராமரிடம் திரும்புகிறார்.","ml":"മഴക്കാലത്ത് രാമൻ മാല്യവാൻ പർവതത്തിൽ കാത്തിരിക്കുന്നു; സുഗ്രീവൻ താമസിക്കുമ്പോൾ ലക്ഷ്മണൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ ഉണർത്തുന്നു; കുരങ്ങന്മാർ എല്ലാ ദിക്കുകളിലും തിരയുന്നു. തെക്കോട്ട് പോയ ഹനുമാന്റെ സംഘം സമ്പാതിയിൽനിന്ന് ലങ്കയെക്കുറിച്ച് അറിയുന്നു; ഹനുമാൻ സമുദ്രം ചാടിക്കടന്ന് സീതയെ കണ്ടെത്തി, നഗരം ചുട്ടെരിച്ച്, അവളുടെ അടയാളവുമായി രാമന്റെ അടുത്തേക്ക് മടങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.266; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"द्रौपदीहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Draupadiharana Parva (Abduction of Draupadi)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"राघवस्तु ससौमित्रिः सुग्रीवेणाभिपालितः ।\nवसन्माल्यवतः पृष्ठे ददर्श विमलं नभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama, with Lakshmana, protected by Sugriva, lived on the spur of Malyavat and looked up at the clear sky."}},{"n":2,"text":"स दृष्ट्वा विमले व्योम्नि निर्मलं शशलक्षणम् ।\nग्रहनक्षत्रताराभिरनुयातममित्रहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that clear sky the destroyer of enemies saw the spotless moon marked with the hare, attended by planets, stars, and constellations."}},{"n":3,"text":"कुमुदोत्पलपद्मानां गन्धमादाय वायुना ।\nमहीधरस्थः शीतेन सहसा प्रतिबोधितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Suddenly, on the mountain, he was awakened by a cool wind carrying the scent of white and blue lotuses and water lilies."}},{"n":4,"text":"प्रभाते लक्ष्मणं वीरमभ्यभाषत दुर्मनाः ।\nसीतां संस्मृत्य धर्मात्मा रुद्धां राक्षसवेश्मनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"At dawn, heavy-hearted, righteous Rama said to the hero Lakshmana, remembering Sita confined in a rakshasa's house:"}},{"n":5,"text":"गच्छ लक्ष्मण जानीहि किष्किन्धायां कपीश्वरम् ।\nप्रमत्तं ग्राम्यधर्मेषु कृतघ्नं स्वार्थपण्डितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Go, Lakshmana, and see the lord of monkeys in Kishkindha, that ungrateful man, clever only for his own gain, absorbed in common pleasures,"}},{"n":6,"text":"योऽसौ कुलाधमो मूढो मया राज्येऽभिषेचितः ।\nसर्ववानरगोपुच्छा यमृक्षाश्च भजन्ति वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"that fool, lowest of his line, whom I consecrated as king, whom all the monkeys and cow-tailed apes and bears attend,"}},{"n":7,"text":"यदर्थं निहतो वाली मया रघुकुलोद्वह ।\nत्वया सह महाबाहो किष्किन्धोपवने तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"for whose sake, O upholder of the Raghus, I once killed Vali with you in the Kishkindha garden."}},{"n":8,"text":"कृतघ्नं तमहं मन्ये वानरापसदं भुवि ।\nयो मामेवंगतो मूढो न जानीतेऽद्य लक्ष्मण ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think him the most ungrateful of monkeys on earth, a fool who, in this state of mine, does not take notice of me today, Lakshmana."}},{"n":9,"text":"असौ मन्ये न जानीते समयप्रतिपादनम् ।\nकृतोपकारं मां नूनमवमन्याल्पया धिया ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think he does not remember the terms of our agreement, and with his petty mind slights me, who did him a favor."}},{"n":10,"text":"यदि तावदनुद्युक्तः शेते कामसुखात्मकः ।\nनेतव्यो वालिमार्गेण सर्वभूतगतिं त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"If he sleeps idle, given to pleasures, then by Vali's path you must lead him to the end of all creatures."}},{"n":11,"text":"अथापि घटतेऽस्माकमर्थे वानरपुंगवः ।\nतमादायैहि काकुत्स्थ त्वरावान्भव मा चिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But if the chief of monkeys is striving for our aim, bring him back with you, Kakutstha; make haste, do not delay.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"इत्युक्तो लक्ष्मणो भ्रात्रा गुरुवाक्यहिते रतः ।\nप्रतस्थे रुचिरं गृह्य समार्गणगुणं धनुः ।\nकिष्किन्धाद्वारमासाद्य प्रविवेशानिवारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus told by his brother, Lakshmana, devoted to his elder's word and welfare, took up his splendid bow with its arrows and set out. He reached the gate of Kishkindha and entered without being stopped."}},{"n":13,"text":"सक्रोध इति तं मत्वा राजा प्रत्युद्ययौ हरिः ।\nतं सदारो विनीतात्मा सुग्रीवः प्लवगाधिपः ।\nपूजया प्रतिजग्राह प्रीयमाणस्तदर्हया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking him angry, Sugriva, king of the monkeys, came out to meet him with his wife, humble, and honored him gladly with fitting courtesy."}},{"n":14,"text":"तमब्रवीद्रामवचः सौमित्रिरकुतोभयः ।\nस तत्सर्वमशेषेण श्रुत्वा प्रह्वः कृताञ्जलिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fearless, the son of Sumitra gave him Rama's message. After hearing all of it, Sugriva bowed humbly with joined hands."}},{"n":15,"text":"सभृत्यदारो राजेन्द्र सुग्रीवो वानराधिपः ।\nइदमाह वचः प्रीतो लक्ष्मणं नरकुञ्जरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sugriva, king of the monkeys, with his servants and wife, glad, said to Lakshmana, the elephant among men:"}},{"n":16,"text":"नास्मि लक्ष्मण दुर्मेधा न कृतघ्नो न निर्घृणः ।\nश्रूयतां यः प्रयत्नो मे सीतापर्येषणे कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Lakshmana, I am not dull, not ungrateful, not pitiless. Hear what effort I have made in the search for Sita."}},{"n":17,"text":"दिशः प्रस्थापिताः सर्वे विनीता हरयो मया ।\nसर्वेषां च कृतः कालो मासेनागमनं पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I sent monkeys, trained, in all directions, and fixed the time for each to come back within a month."}},{"n":18,"text":"यैरियं सवना साद्रिः सपुरा सागराम्बरा ।\nविचेतव्या मही वीर सग्रामनगराकरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those by whom this earth with its forests, mountains, cities, oceans, villages, towns, and mines must be searched, hero,"}},{"n":19,"text":"स मासः पञ्चरात्रेण पूर्णो भवितुमर्हति ।\nततः श्रोष्यसि रामेण सहितः सुमहत्प्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"that month will be complete in five nights. Then, with Rama, you will hear great good news.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"इत्युक्तो लक्ष्मणस्तेन वानरेन्द्रेण धीमता ।\nत्यक्त्वा रोषमदीनात्मा सुग्रीवं प्रत्यपूजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the wise monkey king, Lakshmana put away his anger, and with an untroubled heart honored Sugriva in return."}},{"n":21,"text":"स रामं सहसुग्रीवो माल्यवत्पृष्ठमास्थितम् ।\nअभिगम्योदयं तस्य कार्यस्य प्रत्यवेदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sugriva went with him to Rama on the spur of Malyavat and reported the progress of the work."}},{"n":22,"text":"इत्येवं वानरेन्द्रास्ते समाजग्मुः सहस्रशः ।\nदिशस्तिस्रो विचित्याथ न तु ये दक्षिणां गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So the monkey chiefs came together by thousands after searching three directions, all except those who had gone south."}},{"n":23,"text":"आचख्युस्ते तु रामाय महीं सागरमेखलाम् ।\nविचितां न तु वैदेह्या दर्शनं रावणस्य वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"They told Rama that the earth, girdled by the sea, had been searched, but there was no sight of Sita or Ravana."}},{"n":24,"text":"गतास्तु दक्षिणामाशां ये वै वानरपुंगवाः ।\nआशावांस्तेषु काकुत्स्थः प्राणानार्तोऽप्यधारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama, though afflicted, kept his life by hope in those excellent monkeys who had gone south."}},{"n":25,"text":"द्विमासोपरमे काले व्यतीते प्लवगास्ततः ।\nसुग्रीवमभिगम्येदं त्वरिता वाक्यमब्रुवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When two months had passed, monkeys came hurrying to Sugriva and said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"रक्षितं वालिना यत्तत्स्फीतं मधुवनं महत् ।\nत्वया च प्लवगश्रेष्ठ तद्भुङ्क्ते पवनात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The great, flourishing Madhuvana, once guarded by Vali, and by you, best of monkeys, is being eaten by the son of the wind."}},{"n":27,"text":"वालिपुत्रोऽङ्गदश्चैव ये चान्ये प्लवगर्षभाः ।\nविचेतुं दक्षिणामाशां राजन्प्रस्थापितास्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vali's son Angada and the other bulls among monkeys, whom you sent to search the south, king, are with him.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"तेषां तं प्रणयं श्रुत्वा मेने स कृतकृत्यताम् ।\nकृतार्थानां हि भृत्यानामेतद्भवति चेष्टितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing of their bold liberty, Sugriva concluded that their task was done, for such is the way of servants who have succeeded."}},{"n":29,"text":"स तद्रामाय मेधावी शशंस प्लवगर्षभः ।\nरामश्चाप्यनुमानेन मेने दृष्टां तु मैथिलीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The wise bull among monkeys told Rama, and Rama too guessed that Sita had been found."}},{"n":30,"text":"हनूमत्प्रमुखाश्चापि विश्रान्तास्ते प्लवंगमाः ।\nअभिजग्मुर्हरीन्द्रं तं रामलक्ष्मणसंनिधौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the monkeys led by Hanuman, rested, came before the monkey king in the presence of Rama and Lakshmana."}},{"n":31,"text":"गतिं च मुखवर्णं च दृष्ट्वा रामो हनूमतः ।\nअगमत्प्रत्ययं भूयो दृष्टा सीतेति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Hanuman's gait and the color of his face, Rama grew sure again, O Bharata, that Sita had been seen."}},{"n":32,"text":"हनूमत्प्रमुखास्ते तु वानराः पूर्णमानसाः ।\nप्रणेमुर्विधिवद्रामं सुग्रीवं लक्ष्मणं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The monkeys led by Hanuman, hearts full, bowed properly to Rama, Sugriva, and Lakshmana."}},{"n":33,"text":"तानुवाचागतान्रामः प्रगृह्य सशरं धनुः ।\nअपि मां जीवयिष्यध्वमपि वः कृतकृत्यता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up his bow and arrow, Rama said to them as they stood there: \"Will you restore my life? Is your task done?"}},{"n":34,"text":"अपि राज्यमयोध्यायां कारयिष्याम्यहं पुनः ।\nनिहत्य समरे शत्रूनाहृत्य जनकात्मजाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shall I rule in Ayodhya again, after killing my enemies in battle and bringing back Janaka's daughter?"}},{"n":35,"text":"अमोक्षयित्वा वैदेहीमहत्वा च रिपून्रणे ।\nहृतदारोऽवधूतश्च नाहं जीवितुमुत्सहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without freeing Sita and killing my foes in battle, robbed of my wife and scorned, I cannot bear to live.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"इत्युक्तवचनं रामं प्रत्युवाचानिलात्मजः ।\nप्रियमाख्यामि ते राम दृष्टा सा जानकी मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"To Rama, who had spoken thus, the son of the wind replied: \"I bring you good news, Rama: I have seen Sita."}},{"n":37,"text":"विचित्य दक्षिणामाशां सपर्वतवनाकराम् ।\nश्रान्ताः काले व्यतीते स्म दृष्टवन्तो महागुहाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After searching the southern region with its mountains, forests, and mines, we were tired when the appointed time passed, and then we found a great cave."}},{"n":38,"text":"प्रविशामो वयं तां तु बहुयोजनमायताम् ।\nअन्धकारां सुविपिनां गहनां कीटसेविताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We entered it; it stretched for many yojanas, dark, with thick wilderness, dense and full of insects."}},{"n":39,"text":"गत्वा सुमहदध्वानमादित्यस्य प्रभां ततः ।\nदृष्टवन्तः स्म तत्रैव भवनं दिव्यमन्तरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"After a long distance we saw the light of the sun, and there, in the midst of it, a divine mansion."}},{"n":40,"text":"मयस्य किल दैत्यस्य तदासीद्वेश्म राघव ।\nतत्र प्रभावती नाम तपोऽतप्यत तापसी ॥","meaning":{"en":"That was the house of the daitya Maya, Rama, and there an ascetic woman named Prabhavati was practicing austerities."}},{"n":41,"text":"तया दत्तानि भोज्यानि पानानि विविधानि च ।\nभुक्त्वा लब्धबलाः सन्तस्तयोक्तेन पथा ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"She gave us food and drink of many kinds, and, strengthened by eating, we followed the path she told us and came out of that place."}},{"n":42,"text":"निर्याय तस्मादुद्देशात्पश्यामो लवणाम्भसः ।\nसमीपे सह्यमलयौ दर्दुरं च महागिरिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then we saw the salt sea, with Sahya and Malaya mountains near, and the great mountain Dardura."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततो मलयमारुह्य पश्यन्तो वरुणालयम् ।\nविषण्णा व्यथिताः खिन्ना निराशा जीविते भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Climbing Malaya and looking at the home of Varuna, we were dejected, pained, weary, and almost without hope of life."}},{"n":44,"text":"अनेकशतविस्तीर्णं योजनानां महोदधिम् ।\nतिमिनक्रझषावासं चिन्तयन्तः सुदुःखिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We stared at the huge ocean, many hundreds of yojanas wide, home of timis, crocodiles, and fish, and were deeply sorrowful."}},{"n":45,"text":"तत्रानशनसंकल्पं कृत्वासीना वयं तदा ।\nततः कथान्ते गृध्रस्य जटायोरभवत्कथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we sat down, resolved to fast to death, and as we talked, the story of the vulture Jatayu came up."}},{"n":46,"text":"ततः पर्वतशृङ्गाभं घोररूपं भयावहम् ।\nपक्षिणं दृष्टवन्तः स्म वैनतेयमिवापरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then we saw a frightening bird, big as a mountain peak, like a second Garuda."}},{"n":47,"text":"सोऽस्मानतर्कयद्भोक्तुमथाभ्येत्य वचोऽब्रवीत् ।\nभोः क एष मम भ्रातुर्जटायोः कुरुते कथाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He thought of eating us, came up and said: 'Who is it that speaks of my brother Jatayu?"}},{"n":48,"text":"संपातिर्नाम तस्याहं ज्येष्ठो भ्राता खगाधिपः ।\nअन्योन्यस्पर्धयारूढावावामादित्यसंसदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am Sampati, his elder brother, king of birds. In rivalry we once flew up together toward the sun."}},{"n":49,"text":"ततो दग्धाविमौ पक्षौ न दग्धौ तु जटायुषः ।\nतदा मे चिरदृष्टः स भ्राता गृध्रपतिः प्रियः ।\nनिर्दग्धपक्षः पतितो ह्यहमस्मिन्महागिरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both my wings were burned, but Jatayu's were not. Then I did not see my dear brother, king of vultures, for a long time; I, my wings burned, fell on this great mountain.'"}},{"n":50,"text":"तस्यैवं वदतोऽस्माभिर्हतो भ्राता निवेदितः ।\nव्यसनं भवतश्चेदं संक्षेपाद्वै निवेदितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We told him, as he spoke, that his brother had been killed, and we briefly told him of your trouble too."}},{"n":51,"text":"स संपातिस्तदा राजञ्श्रुत्वा सुमहदप्रियम् ।\nविषण्णचेताः पप्रच्छ पुनरस्मानरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this very unwelcome news, Sampati, sad at heart, asked us again, tamer of foes:"}},{"n":52,"text":"कः स रामः कथं सीता जटायुश्च कथं हतः ।\nइच्छामि सर्वमेवैतच्छ्रोतुं प्लवगसत्तमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Who is this Rama? How did Sita come to be lost, and how was Jatayu killed? I want to hear everything, best of monkeys.'"}},{"n":53,"text":"तस्याहं सर्वमेवैतं भवतो व्यसनागमम् ।\nप्रायोपवेशने चैव हेतुं विस्तरतोऽब्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I told him everything about your misfortune and the reason for our fasting to death, in detail."}},{"n":54,"text":"सोऽस्मानुत्थापयामास वाक्येनानेन पक्षिराट् ।\nरावणो विदितो मह्यं लङ्का चास्य महापुरी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of birds made us get up with these words: 'I know Ravana, and his great city Lanka."}},{"n":55,"text":"दृष्टा पारे समुद्रस्य त्रिकूटगिरिकन्दरे ।\nभवित्री तत्र वैदेही न मेऽस्त्यत्र विचारणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have seen it across the sea, in a cave of Mount Trikuta. Sita must be there; I have no doubt about this.'"}},{"n":56,"text":"इति तस्य वचः श्रुत्वा वयमुत्थाय सत्वराः ।\nसागरप्लवने मन्त्रं मन्त्रयामः परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, we got up quickly, and we took counsel about crossing the sea, tamer of foes."}},{"n":57,"text":"नाध्यवस्यद्यदा कश्चित्सागरस्य विलङ्घने ।\nततः पितरमाविश्य पुप्लुवेऽहं महार्णवम् ।\nशतयोजनविस्तीर्णं निहत्य जलराक्षसीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When no one had the resolve to leap over the ocean, I entered my father's strength and leapt over the great ocean, a hundred yojanas wide, killing a sea-rakshasi on the way."}},{"n":58,"text":"तत्र सीता मया दृष्टा रावणान्तःपुरे सती ।\nउपवासतपःशीला भर्तृदर्शनलालसा ।\nजटिला मलदिग्धाङ्गी कृशा दीना तपस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"There I saw Sita, the faithful wife, in Ravana's inner quarters, fasting and austere, longing to see her husband, with matted hair, her limbs smeared with dirt, thin, wretched, an ascetic."}},{"n":59,"text":"निमित्तैस्तामहं सीतामुपलभ्य पृथग्विधैः ।\nउपसृत्याब्रुवं चार्यामभिगम्य रहोगताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having recognized Sita by various signs, I went to her in private and said to her, noble lady:"}},{"n":60,"text":"सीते रामस्य दूतोऽहं वानरो मारुतात्मजः ।\nत्वद्दर्शनमभिप्रेप्सुरिह प्राप्तो विहायसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"'Sita, I am Rama's messenger, a monkey, son of the wind. Wanting to see you, I have come here through the sky."}},{"n":61,"text":"राजपुत्रौ कुशलिनौ भ्रातरौ रामलक्ष्मणौ ।\nसर्वशाखामृगेन्द्रेण सुग्रीवेणाभिपालितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two princes, the brothers Rama and Lakshmana, are well, and protected by Sugriva, king of all monkeys."}},{"n":62,"text":"कुशलं त्वाब्रवीद्रामः सीते सौमित्रिणा सह ।\nसखिभावाच्च सुग्रीवः कुशलं त्वानुपृच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama sends his good wishes to you, Sita, with Lakshmana, and out of friendship Sugriva too asks after your welfare."}},{"n":63,"text":"क्षिप्रमेष्यति ते भर्ता सर्वशाखामृगैः सह ।\nप्रत्ययं कुरु मे देवि वानरोऽस्मि न राक्षसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your husband will come soon with all the monkeys. Trust me, lady; I am a monkey, not a rakshasa.'"}},{"n":64,"text":"मुहूर्तमिव च ध्यात्वा सीता मां प्रत्युवाच ह ।\nअवैमि त्वां हनूमन्तमविन्ध्यवचनादहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sita thought for a moment and then replied: 'I know you are Hanuman from Avindhya's words."}},{"n":65,"text":"अविन्ध्यो हि महाबाहो राक्षसो वृद्धसंमतः ।\nकथितस्तेन सुग्रीवस्त्वद्विधैः सचिवैर्वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Avindhya, mighty man, is a rakshasa respected by the elders; he told me about Sugriva, surrounded by ministers like you.'"}},{"n":66,"text":"गम्यतामिति चोक्त्वा मां सीता प्रादादिमं मणिम् ।\nधारिता येन वैदेही कालमेतमनिन्दिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"She told me 'Go' and gave me this jewel, by which the blameless Sita has kept herself alive all this time."}},{"n":67,"text":"प्रत्ययार्थं कथां चेमां कथयामास जानकी ।\nक्षिप्तामिषीकां काकस्य चित्रकूटे महागिरौ ।\nभवता पुरुषव्याघ्र प्रत्यभिज्ञानकारणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a token, Janaki also told this story: how you, tiger among men, hurled a blade of grass at a crow on the great mountain Chitrakuta, as a sign for recognition."}},{"n":68,"text":"श्रावयित्वा तदात्मानं ततो दग्ध्वा च तां पुरीम् ।\nसंप्राप्त इति तं रामः प्रियवादिनमर्चयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made myself known, I burned that city, and I have come back.\" Rama honored him, who spoke so kindly."}}]}]}